# Super-repo ignores. Source lives in the submodules; this repo holds pins, orchestration scripts and
# dev manifests, so there was nothing generated to ignore until now. Checked-in agent config
# (.claude/settings.json, .cursor/rules/, opencode.json) is deliberate and stays tracked.

# Qoder's generated repo wiki: ~1.7 MB of Markdown re-derived from the submodules and rewritten
# wholesale on each run. Committing it would park a stale copy of the Source of Truth inside the repo
# that defers to governance for every decision (invariant 21), and it would show up as churn in every
# diff that touches a submodule. .mimocode/ solves the same problem with a .gitignore that hides its
# own contents; .qoder/ ships none, and such a file would not survive its wipe-and-regenerate anyway,
# so the pattern belongs here.
.qoder/

# Default output of scripts/bench-storage.sh (T-0007). Runs are archived under
# governance/docs/bench/ with the result doc that interprets them; a stray local run should not
# look like tracked evidence.
/bench-results/

# Per-developer agent tooling. `.claude/settings.json`, `.claude/agents/` and `.cursor/rules/` are
# deliberately tracked (the agents are generated — ADR-0037); everything else under these paths is
# whatever plugins a given developer has installed, and it has no business in a shared repo.
#
# This exists because 13 such files were committed by a `git add -A` in 782854f and then blocked a
# `git pull` on the machine they came from — the tree they were swept out of could no longer take
# its own files back. Naming the paths is cheaper than remembering not to stage them.
.claude/commands/
.claude/skills/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.json.*-bak
.claude/worktrees/
.codex/
.cursor/commands/
.cursor/skills/
.github/prompts/
.github/skills/
openspec/
